# The proposal names a platform Highway has not onboarded. Onboarding hands its decision,
# architecture, and implementation to their owners, then the original visit resumes at execution.
id: implementation-onboards-platform
skill: highway-implementation
through: highway-onboarding
through: highway-adr
through: highway-architecture
fixture: architecture
open: /highway-implementation for the Scheduled Restock Alert Service architecture. A scheduled job runs every Monday, calls the order service stock query with a read-only token, and emails the warehouse lead. It is not a code project, so Language is None. It is not running yet.
ask-pattern: Here are the capabilities Highway believes you have today
say: [edit] Remove AI-Augmented Technology Development.
ask: What should this architecture be called?
say: Self-Hosted Build and Scheduled Job Automation
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [edit] Deployed by and Managed by are Jenkins. We build, deploy, and run scheduled jobs with Jenkins on our own build servers.
ask-pattern: Would you like to configure how highway-codify uses
say: [decline] Not now.
ask-pattern: Would you like to configure how highway-codify uses
say: [decline] Not now.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
ask: What would you add, correct, or remove?
say: [accept] Looks good.
